ithmetic until they land\r\n  · whether a finding a detector raised is already known and accepted: dismissals are `e4.6`'s, so a score counts every finding it can see\r\n  · whether the tests that arrived assert anything: coverage shape is measurable, coverage quality is not, and this model does not pretend otherwise\r\n  · whether a dependency is stale or vulnerable: advisory age is `e2.7`'s, behind `net-advisories` and a consent flag, and a score that moved with the network would not be reproducible\r\n  · whether the human reviewing this has already read it: review state is a queue's business (`e4.5`), not a feature's\r\n"]
